onfig.ConfigError` ... so does any failure to read the committed file\"","_config_sources.py:129-132 reads TOML in binary mode and maps TOMLDecodeError (which covers invalid UTF-8) to ConfigError"],"finding":"Strict `encoding=\"utf-8\"` turns the plan's own named failure (a byte in the committed `rebar.toml` that is not valid UTF-8) into an uncaught `UnicodeDecodeError` instead of the `ConfigError` the module promises. `UnicodeDecodeError` is a `ValueError`. `_git()` catches only `(OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError)` and `_committed_toml` catches only `tomllib.TOMLDecodeError`, so the decode error escapes both as a raw traceback. The working-tree reader (`_config_sources._parse_toml`, binary `tomllib.load`) maps the same bad input to `ConfigError`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2cbb01fb134b2034","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix section / src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:58-69 (_git) and :106-112 (_committed_toml)","norm_id":"n17f7b126145e79be","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A committed base-branch `rebar.toml` or `pyproject.toml` is saved in cp1252 (for example an em-dash byte 0x97 in a comment). `rebar verify-opcert` then crashes with a UnicodeDecodeError traceback instead of reporting a ConfigError that names the bad spec.","git writes non-UTF-8 bytes to stderr (for example a localized message under a legacy code page). The decode error then hides the real git failure."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In `_git()`, widen the except clause to `except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, UnicodeDecodeError) as exc:` so it keeps raising `ConfigError(f\"op-cert gate: git {args[0]} failed in {root}: {exc}\")`. Add a test that commits a `rebar.toml` containing byte 0x97 on `origin/main` and asserts that `gate_config()` raises `ConfigError`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_refe